WEBVTT

00:01.918 --> 00:02.919
You...

00:03.545 --> 00:05.839
What do you know about my family?

00:07.215 --> 00:09.092
I'm not obligated to answer that.

00:09.175 --> 00:12.387
But as a veteran of the underworld,
I'll tell you one thing.

00:13.388 --> 00:16.975
This world is littered
with scores of hidden truths.

00:18.435 --> 00:21.813
Taiyo, we have an emergency on our hands.
Watch the video.

00:22.731 --> 00:24.524
<i>The deputy prime minister's been abducted,</i>

00:24.607 --> 00:26.860
<i>and he's being live-streamed</i>
<i>from somewhere.</i>

00:26.943 --> 00:30.864
He was switched with a surrogate
in the middle of the chaos earlier.

00:30.947 --> 00:33.575
He must have been their target all along.

00:33.992 --> 00:36.870
<i>Interrogate Kuroyuri right now,</i>
<i>and get him to cough up the location.</i>

00:36.953 --> 00:38.621
How convenient.

00:39.539 --> 00:43.293
As I was just about to head over
to the abduction site myself.

00:43.918 --> 00:45.003
What?

01:02.854 --> 01:09.444
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

02:26.354 --> 02:31.025
PLAN 9
THE FLOWER MEANING OF KUROYURI

02:32.819 --> 02:33.820
Oh.

02:39.159 --> 02:40.827
Are you okay, Nanao?

02:41.327 --> 02:42.704
What on earth happened?

02:43.580 --> 02:45.248
I'm sorry.

02:45.331 --> 02:50.086
I messed up the ratio of ingredients
and destroyed the inside of this room.

02:50.170 --> 02:54.048
I think you're in worse shape
than the inside of the room, Nanao.

02:57.886 --> 03:02.849
The thing is, just thinking that
Big Bro Taiyo could get hurt on a mission

03:02.932 --> 03:05.351
makes me so anxious, I can't sit still.

03:05.435 --> 03:06.686
Nanao...

03:06.769 --> 03:12.400
So, in case he comes home looking like
a frog's corpse run over by a car,

03:12.483 --> 03:14.944
I'm concocting a really effective potion
to heal him up.

03:15.028 --> 03:18.323
If he's a "frog's corpse,"
that means he'd already be dead, right?

03:18.740 --> 03:21.284
Aren't you worried,
Big Sis Mutsumi?

03:21.367 --> 03:23.912
Of course. I'm totally worried.

03:24.537 --> 03:27.999
But since there's
no use brooding over it...

03:28.082 --> 03:29.083
GREAT WORK, TAIYO

03:30.084 --> 03:32.754
...what else can I do
but prepare a feast and wait for him?

03:33.838 --> 03:36.216
Even if he comes back
hurt somehow,

03:36.299 --> 03:38.927
he should recover right away
once he eats all this, right?

03:39.010 --> 03:43.223
No, he'll probably end up hurting
somewhere else if he eats all this.

03:44.098 --> 03:47.685
Come to think of it,
what's everybody else up to?

03:48.770 --> 03:50.396
<i>Well, Big Bro Kengo</i>

03:50.480 --> 03:55.568
<i>is working on a machine-washable face</i>
<i>for Big Bro Taiyo to use</i>

03:55.652 --> 03:58.446
<i>if he comes home unrecognizable.</i>

03:58.947 --> 04:01.991
<i>So he's assuming</i>
<i>that he won't be all right.</i>

04:04.535 --> 04:08.122
<i>Big Sis Shion is taking out</i>
<i>all our haters' computers</i>

04:08.206 --> 04:12.335
<i>so they won't cause a commotion</i>
<i>if something happens to Big Bro Taiyo.</i>

04:12.418 --> 04:15.296
<i>Isn't that her</i>
<i>just being spiteful?</i>

04:18.341 --> 04:22.637
<i>Big Bro Shinzo is so worried</i>
<i>that he's an emotional basket case.</i>

04:22.720 --> 04:24.806
<i>He's been holed up this whole time.</i>

04:24.889 --> 04:28.726
<i>If the ones staying home</i>
<i>have lost it, we're in real trouble!</i>

04:35.358 --> 04:39.279
Oh, wow, neither one
of them has moved a muscle.

04:39.362 --> 04:42.490
Well, there's no need
to worry, right?

04:42.991 --> 04:45.034
That kid can get things done
when he has to.

04:45.118 --> 04:46.661
Big Sis Futaba!

04:46.744 --> 04:50.873
Actually, just imagining
how gruesome a demise he'll meet

04:50.957 --> 04:52.667
makes my tea taste even better.

04:54.585 --> 04:56.170
I'd call this fun rather than worrisome!

04:56.254 --> 04:58.131
<i>That's</i> what
you're thinking?!

05:12.854 --> 05:16.399
Hide Asano, Akari Asano,
Hikaru Asano...

05:16.899 --> 05:20.069
One rainy day,
they fell off a cliff, car and all.

05:20.820 --> 05:23.698
<i>Your family died instantly,</i>
<i>but you alone survived.</i>

05:23.781 --> 05:25.616
<i>Truly miraculous.</i>

05:25.700 --> 05:26.909
<i>However...</i>

05:27.535 --> 05:32.915
some miracles are the handiwork of man.

05:37.628 --> 05:39.255
<i>Are you all right, Taiyo?</i>

05:39.756 --> 05:42.216
Y-Yeah. Just barely.

05:43.009 --> 05:46.387
The driver survived,
but Kuroyuri got away from me.

05:46.846 --> 05:49.140
<i>No problem. We expected that.</i>

05:49.223 --> 05:50.224
Huh?

05:50.475 --> 05:52.643
I chose to keep this from you,

05:52.727 --> 05:55.772
but that guy
isn't just a cultish politician.

05:56.689 --> 05:58.399
He's a spy, just like us.

05:59.650 --> 06:02.236
<i>Kuroyuri's former alias was Kurogao.</i>

06:02.945 --> 06:06.532
<i>Back then, he was a legendary spy</i>
<i>working in the shadows around the world.</i>

06:07.742 --> 06:10.495
He was thought to have died
five or six years ago,

06:10.578 --> 06:12.372
but as you can see, he's alive and well.

06:12.872 --> 06:14.832
We eased security on him
and left him at large...

06:14.916 --> 06:17.377
<i>so that we could find out</i>
<i>what he was up to.</i>

06:17.460 --> 06:18.795
So I was just the bait?

06:19.253 --> 06:21.798
Fortunately, we can rescue
the deputy prime minister

06:21.881 --> 06:24.133
by using the GPS tracker
we planted on him.

06:24.592 --> 06:26.344
<i>You can return to headquarters now.</i>

06:29.889 --> 06:33.768
This world is littered
with scores of hidden truths.

06:42.735 --> 06:44.278
Good afternoon.

06:44.695 --> 06:46.072
Kuroyuri?

06:47.156 --> 06:48.157
What is this?

06:48.241 --> 06:49.242
Oh, relax.

06:50.118 --> 06:53.121
<i>I've set up a venue</i>
<i>for us to have a heart-to-heart.</i>

06:53.579 --> 06:56.624
<i>-The media must be in an uproar right now.</i>
<i>-</i>

06:57.208 --> 06:59.085
You were
an oddball of a politician,

06:59.168 --> 07:00.837
but I always thought you were committed.

07:00.920 --> 07:05.049
I'm disappointed to see that you're
nothing but an immature terrorist.

07:05.466 --> 07:08.553
Pulling this kind of stunt
won't change the political climate!

07:08.636 --> 07:11.264
I have no interest whatsoever in politics.

07:11.347 --> 07:12.348
What?

07:12.432 --> 07:13.766
You still don't get it?

07:14.267 --> 07:15.685
Well, not that I blame you.

07:16.185 --> 07:19.313
The essence of disguise is to deceive
not the eyes, but the soul.

07:19.814 --> 07:23.317
If you think, "No way
could he be standing before my eyes,"

07:23.401 --> 07:27.280
you'd never notice him,
even if his looks hadn't changed at all.

07:28.197 --> 07:32.577
All the more if it's someone
you're sure that you've killed!

07:34.495 --> 07:35.496
Kurogao?

07:35.997 --> 07:38.166
Now, let's begin our conversation.

07:38.666 --> 07:41.669
I'll be speaking
not as the leader of the Kuroyuri Party,

07:41.752 --> 07:43.963
<i>but as a father who's lost his child.</i>

07:46.215 --> 07:47.425
<i>I...</i>

07:48.426 --> 07:52.680
<i>I've inflicted vengeance</i>
<i>on numerous politicians behind the scenes.</i>

07:53.806 --> 07:57.226
<i>But since you're the only one</i>
<i>who knows the whole story...</i>

07:59.270 --> 08:02.398
<i>I wanted to do the deed in broad daylight.</i>

08:04.025 --> 08:06.235
So, time for the interview.

08:06.861 --> 08:10.823
Are you going to speak the truth
and be obliterated by society

08:10.907 --> 08:15.077
or refuse to confess
and choose to die physically?

08:15.161 --> 08:17.205
The truth, eh?

08:17.705 --> 08:20.374
If I were one to blurt out the truth
so heedlessly,

08:20.458 --> 08:22.168
I would be a failure as a politician.

08:23.085 --> 08:24.629
I thought as much.

08:26.839 --> 08:28.132
<i>Farewell.</i>

08:29.592 --> 08:31.802
-The stream got cut off!
-What's going on?

08:40.269 --> 08:42.063
Good of you to come, young man.

08:42.563 --> 08:44.273
Let the deputy prime minister go!

08:44.774 --> 08:47.109
It's no use. You can't shoot me.

08:47.818 --> 08:50.071
The Yozakura
Electric Revolver Yae

08:50.154 --> 08:53.824
expands its power and range
in proportion to its output.

08:54.200 --> 08:57.245
At this distance,
that range is a four-meter radius.

08:57.745 --> 09:00.873
If you fire now, this guy
will end up in the crossfire for sure.

09:00.957 --> 09:03.751
Your bargaining skills need work.

09:06.003 --> 09:09.006
<i>The moment right after your</i>
<i>opponent's attack is your starting signal.</i>

09:09.090 --> 09:11.008
<i>Close the distance as quickly as possible,</i>

09:11.092 --> 09:13.469
<i>and match your moves</i>
<i>to your opponent's form!</i>

09:15.513 --> 09:16.764
<i>Got him!</i>

09:17.515 --> 09:19.267
The Yozakura-style
jiujitsu move...

09:19.350 --> 09:21.060
...Cascading Kumite, eh?

09:24.522 --> 09:27.608
The greater the difference in physique,
the more effective it is.

09:27.692 --> 09:30.528
It's currently wielded
by the eldest daughter, Futaba.

09:31.696 --> 09:36.242
Steel and carbon fiber wires
are also time-honored Yozakura techniques.

09:38.786 --> 09:40.496
I'll help myself to them now.

09:41.372 --> 09:43.958
<i>How does he know? How can he?</i>

09:44.625 --> 09:47.503
"How do I know all about
the Yozakura battle techniques?"

09:47.587 --> 09:49.297
says the look on your face.

09:51.007 --> 09:54.010
I may not have
any special martial arts skills,

09:54.093 --> 09:57.179
but I am rather well-versed
in handling information.

09:57.263 --> 09:59.473
For a spy, nothing is
more vital than information.

09:59.557 --> 10:02.893
But if all you can do is gather
information, you're second-rate.

10:03.311 --> 10:07.023
Only when you're able to fully exploit
that information do you truly come alive.

10:07.106 --> 10:08.107
Why...

10:08.733 --> 10:11.527
Why would a spy like you turn politician

10:11.611 --> 10:14.155
just to use vile means
to deceive ordinary people?

10:14.655 --> 10:19.577
Young man, like I said before,
I have no interest in politics.

10:19.660 --> 10:21.078
Then why?

10:22.330 --> 10:23.581
For revenge.

10:24.790 --> 10:28.169
Thanks to my ability
to exploit information,

10:28.252 --> 10:30.963
I was prized in the political world.

10:33.633 --> 10:35.968
Yes. Even then.

10:37.428 --> 10:40.431
I'm sending you the accounting data
in the hidden folder.

10:40.848 --> 10:41.974
<i>Good job.</i>

10:42.475 --> 10:44.477
<i>Now lie low until your next directive.</i>

10:44.977 --> 10:45.978
Roger that.

11:02.662 --> 11:05.790
Happy birthday, Yuri!

11:09.460 --> 11:12.171
Overworking has turned you
into a weirdo, Daddy.

11:12.254 --> 11:17.301
Wait, no! Sorry.
I just wanted to make you happy.

11:18.969 --> 11:20.763
I'm sorry too!

11:20.846 --> 11:24.392
Ever since Mom died, you've always
been away on business trips.

11:24.475 --> 11:27.186
I've missed you so much,
I just felt like being mean for a second.

11:28.771 --> 11:30.439
Thanks for coming home!

11:30.940 --> 11:32.983
Let's have that cake together!

11:33.693 --> 11:34.694
Yuri...

11:35.277 --> 11:38.155
Oh, but if you're going to surprise me,
do it right, okay?

11:38.239 --> 11:40.700
Sending me my present first
is a dead giveaway, right?

11:40.783 --> 11:41.951
Present?

12:04.557 --> 12:05.641
Yuri!

12:16.110 --> 12:19.071
<i>I'd served my purpose,</i>
<i>and so they jettisoned me.</i>

12:20.614 --> 12:22.658
<i>I've murdered scores of people.</i>

12:23.159 --> 12:25.286
<i>I'm not going to start</i>
<i>preaching right and wrong.</i>

12:26.454 --> 12:29.957
<i>But I had to drive it home to them...</i>

12:30.750 --> 12:34.795
<i>what it means to antagonize me.</i>

12:36.756 --> 12:41.010
So faking your own death
and putting on the fake politician act,

12:41.093 --> 12:44.722
that was all motivated
by your thirst for revenge against us?

12:44.805 --> 12:47.850
Yes. And after actually
becoming a politician,

12:47.933 --> 12:49.894
it was laughably easy
to reel in your comrades

12:49.977 --> 12:52.897
using my achievements
and approval ratings as bait.

12:52.980 --> 12:55.399
There was nothing wrong with my strategy.

12:56.108 --> 13:00.196
You're the last man standing,
Deputy Prime Minister Shirasagi.

13:08.788 --> 13:11.916
Give it up.
You don't stand a chance on your own.

13:12.291 --> 13:16.504
Young man, I'm sure that
you know the pain of losing your family.

13:16.587 --> 13:20.090
As a kindred spirit of mine,
I don't want to hurt you for no reason.

13:20.174 --> 13:22.259
If you agree to step back now,

13:22.343 --> 13:26.472
I'll tell you all that I know
about your family.

13:27.556 --> 13:30.059
I don't need you to tell me about them.

13:31.018 --> 13:32.937
I do understand
where you're coming from,

13:33.020 --> 13:36.607
and if there are what you called
"hidden truths" behind that accident,

13:36.690 --> 13:38.526
then I do want to know
what really happened.

13:39.318 --> 13:40.444
But above all...

13:41.695 --> 13:43.781
I don't want any more people to die.

13:47.743 --> 13:48.744
That's all!

13:56.085 --> 13:57.795
Hinagiku...

13:58.420 --> 14:00.214
I'll take care of the others.

14:00.756 --> 14:03.384
Make sure you arrest the suspect
and rescue that man.

14:03.884 --> 14:04.885
Roger that.

14:16.981 --> 14:19.692
As I'd expect of Hinagiku. How flashy.

14:22.152 --> 14:26.532
This unique hollow tells me that it's
a battle knife made by Shinzo.

14:26.907 --> 14:29.368
One can load poison into this hollow.

14:29.451 --> 14:30.828
For example...

14:32.538 --> 14:35.833
...something like a muscle relaxant
developed by Dr. Nanao!

14:48.053 --> 14:50.514
You don't want anyone
to die, huh?

14:51.140 --> 14:52.516
Don't be naive!

14:52.850 --> 14:56.854
People die. Just like my own daughter...

15:06.113 --> 15:08.282
Impressive, Hinagiku Squad Leader.

15:08.365 --> 15:10.242
You have some skill with a sword.

15:10.326 --> 15:13.787
But can a government dog contain us,
I wonder?

15:14.288 --> 15:15.539
Red Flames.

15:16.457 --> 15:18.667
I specialize in arson
and acts of terrorism.

15:19.376 --> 15:20.586
Blue Water.

15:21.211 --> 15:24.089
I can slash anything
from human bodies to hard disks.

15:25.257 --> 15:26.675
Yellow Lightning.

15:27.635 --> 15:30.262
I rewrite both data and brains
and destroy them.

15:31.388 --> 15:34.224
When we work
as a team, we're unstoppable.

15:34.308 --> 15:36.518
RED BLUE YELLOW
SPY FAMILY RANKING: 5TH

15:37.019 --> 15:38.979
Revealing your own information.

15:39.480 --> 15:41.023
How arrogant.

15:41.106 --> 15:43.359
Then allow me to reveal one thing to you.

15:44.068 --> 15:46.195
The foundation
of the Hinagiku combat style

15:46.278 --> 15:48.364
is the moving technique
Walking on Flowers.

15:49.198 --> 15:51.450
<i>Like flower petals</i>
<i>fluttering down to the ground,</i>

15:51.533 --> 15:54.620
<i>you absorb all sound and resistance</i>
<i>by treading lightly...</i>

15:55.371 --> 15:58.332
<i>making it possible to move</i>
<i>soundlessly and swiftly.</i>

15:59.625 --> 16:03.545
It's just a basic move that anyone
can master once they get the hang of it,

16:03.629 --> 16:06.715
but its flexibility
can also be applied to sword skills.

16:07.424 --> 16:09.927
If you're confident enough,
let's see you stay out of range.

16:10.761 --> 16:12.721
Who's the arrogant one here?

16:13.222 --> 16:14.431
You'll regret this.

16:16.725 --> 16:18.185
Primary Colors!

16:23.857 --> 16:25.317
<i>Narcissus-style Sword Skill...</i>

16:30.781 --> 16:32.199
<i>Underwater Blossom.</i>

16:37.663 --> 16:38.956
<i>So strong.</i>

16:47.631 --> 16:49.842
<i>Taiyo won't last much longer.</i>

16:50.676 --> 16:51.760
<i>I need to get back up--</i>

17:01.311 --> 17:02.980
<i>What was that presence?</i>

17:06.483 --> 17:09.611
You've lost your family,
so you should know.

17:09.695 --> 17:12.364
The never-ending pain,
the despair that won't go away.

17:13.032 --> 17:15.159
There's nothing that you can change,

17:15.242 --> 17:17.953
not your harsh reality nor this situation.

17:18.037 --> 17:19.496
I agree.

17:19.872 --> 17:21.582
You're right.

17:21.665 --> 17:22.666
ASANO FAMILY GRAVE

17:22.750 --> 17:27.171
<i>All this time, that's how</i>
<i>I've felt as I went through life.</i>

17:28.047 --> 17:29.048
<i>But...</i>

17:42.061 --> 17:43.228
<i>...not anymore.</i>

17:45.773 --> 17:48.609
Reality isn't something
you just have to accept.

17:48.692 --> 17:50.402
There are also things you can change!

17:51.361 --> 17:53.906
That's what I was taught!

17:55.199 --> 17:57.242
<i>Smoke screens, explosives,</i>

17:57.326 --> 17:59.078
<i>nine techniques, tops.</i>

17:59.620 --> 18:02.539
<i>I have all of your information</i>
<i>in the palm of my hand.</i>

18:03.582 --> 18:05.292
<i>Taiyo Asano...</i>

18:12.341 --> 18:13.342
<i>That's...</i>

18:14.843 --> 18:17.763
<i>the Hinagiku-style movement skill,</i>
<i>Walking on Flowers!</i>

18:18.555 --> 18:20.349
<i>How is he able to do it?</i>

18:21.517 --> 18:23.018
<i>I've said this before.</i>

18:23.102 --> 18:24.812
<i>Spies engage in wars of intel.</i>

18:25.604 --> 18:28.065
A pro would already know
everything about you.

18:28.148 --> 18:30.567
None of your attacks would work on him.

18:30.984 --> 18:36.198
But the arrogance of "knowing" can blunt
one's ability to handle the unexpected.

18:36.949 --> 18:38.325
<i>It doesn't have to be perfect.</i>

18:38.408 --> 18:39.868
<i>It can be a mere stopgap.</i>

18:39.993 --> 18:43.080
<i>As long as you trust the information</i>
<i>ingrained in your body...</i>

18:43.580 --> 18:45.249
<i>you can turn the tides!</i>

18:49.253 --> 18:52.464
<i>Nanao's antidote, embedded</i>
<i>in his tooth, gives him a speed boost.</i>

18:53.632 --> 18:56.969
<i>Shion's combat tactics data</i>
<i>analyzes the knife's trajectory.</i>

18:58.220 --> 19:00.472
<i>Kengo's protective fake skin</i>
<i>neutralizes the blow.</i>

19:01.765 --> 19:04.268
<i>Futaba's jiujitsu skills</i>
<i>move him out of shooting range.</i>

19:05.811 --> 19:09.439
<i>Shinzo's jamming gum disarms the weapon.</i>

19:10.315 --> 19:12.693
<i>Even with my spare gun...</i>

19:16.738 --> 19:20.534
<i>Kyoichiro's Steel Spider</i>
<i>means this is checkmate!</i>

19:26.331 --> 19:29.459
<i>To think that information</i>
<i>would be my downfall.</i>

19:31.295 --> 19:35.007
You beat me hands down.
You're something else, young man.

19:35.090 --> 19:39.511
As someone who's given up on everything,
I was always destined to end up this way.

19:40.512 --> 19:43.432
But you, on the other hand,
you refused to give up.

19:43.515 --> 19:45.893
You chose to struggle
through your hardship.

19:46.435 --> 19:51.815
Out of respect for your mental resilience,
let me tell you all that I know.

19:51.899 --> 19:52.900
Uh?

19:54.026 --> 19:55.027
Your--

20:00.574 --> 20:01.617
<i>Huh?</i>

20:03.202 --> 20:04.536
<i>A bullet wound?</i>

20:05.621 --> 20:07.331
<i>But where did it come from?</i>

20:09.499 --> 20:10.584
You must...

20:11.251 --> 20:14.588
move on without fear...

20:28.060 --> 20:29.311
Kurogao...

20:29.978 --> 20:32.314
He must have been
silenced by an assassin.

20:32.981 --> 20:35.692
You may not have been able
to achieve your goal,

20:35.776 --> 20:39.029
but for now, you should be proud
that you carried out your mission.

20:39.613 --> 20:42.741
To take pride in one's success
is a survivor's duty,

20:43.116 --> 20:45.369
as well as a way to honor the dead.

20:56.505 --> 21:00.968
<i>On the spot that I've marked</i>
<i>on this map, you'll find a single tree.</i>

21:02.094 --> 21:03.637
<i>I laid my daughter to rest here</i>

21:03.720 --> 21:07.683
<i>so that she could see the beach</i>
<i>where we often played together.</i>

21:11.603 --> 21:13.230
<i>I'd like you to lay some white lilies,</i>

21:13.313 --> 21:15.232
<i>her favorite flowers,</i>
<i>on her resting place.</i>

21:18.694 --> 21:22.364
<i>And inside a small knothole...</i>

21:22.864 --> 21:25.409
<i>you'll find what you're seeking.</i>

21:40.132 --> 21:41.133
Uh?

21:47.222 --> 21:49.725
-I'm home--
-Welcome home, Taiyo!

21:51.476 --> 21:53.020
Good work, Taiyo!

21:55.188 --> 21:56.273
Good job!

21:56.356 --> 21:57.524
Welcome home!

21:58.150 --> 22:00.902
-Welcome home, Taiyo!
-You did great, Taiyo!

22:02.696 --> 22:05.490
What do you look so disappointed about,
idiot firstborn?

22:07.326 --> 22:09.161
Why are you crying,
Big Bro Shinzo?

22:09.244 --> 22:11.330
Thank goodness!

22:12.164 --> 22:13.206
So annoying!

22:13.290 --> 22:14.750
I'm so relieved!

22:14.833 --> 22:15.959
Hey, don't fight!

23:46.633 --> 23:50.887
NEXT TIME
THE YOZAKURA FAMILY MAID/AFFAIR
